data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/mission_reply.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign summary: greet, tested\\n\\nDispatched d002 to dev with the exact mission requirements. Dev delivered\\n`src/greet.py` (greet(name) -\u003e \\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\") and `tests/test_greet.py`\\n(covers a normal name and the empty string) in one pass, committed to its own\\nbranch (cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>, commit 1236384).\\n\\nI independently verified rather than trusting the report: fetched dev's\\nbranch, checked out the exact commit into an isolated worktree, and ran\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself — 2 tests, exit code 0.\\nAccepted d002.\\n\\nAll three stated criteria (greet.py behavior, test coverage of both cases,\\nclean unittest discovery run) are satisfied. Durable report written to\\n~/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-report.md.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

